course: dictionary
lesson: 3392
title: Expecting: waiting, predicting, or having a baby
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Expecting means waiting for something to arrive, or thinking something will probably happen. «I'm expecting a parcel» means you are waiting for it to come. «We're expecting rain» means you think rain will probably fall, so take a coat.
explain: The clues around the word tell you which meaning is right. A parcel, rain, or a baby each point to a different sense. Read the whole sentence before you decide, and then try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
explain: Grown-ups sometimes use expecting to mean that a baby is growing inside a mum. It is a polite, everyday word for pregnant. The example «Pregnancy has many soft and funny names, from the polite "expecting" to the joking "a bun in the oven".» shows that people choose different words for the same idea.
fact: Expecting means waiting for something, or thinking something will probably happen.
fact: «Expecting» can also mean pregnant, a polite way of saying a baby is growing inside a mum.
fact: In maths and science, the expected answer is the answer you predict before you work it out.
fact: Expect, expects, expected and expecting all come from the same verb.
fact: Context tells you which meaning is right: a parcel, rain, or a baby.
exercise: «I'm expecting a parcel this afternoon.» What does expecting mean here? | Hiding from visitors | *Waiting for something to arrive | Shouting at the postman | Feeling very sleepy
exercise: «We're expecting rain, so take a coat.» What does expecting mean here? | Drying the washing | Splashing in puddles | Wishing for a sunny day | *Thinking rain will probably happen
exercise: In maths, Ravi asks, «What is the expected answer?» What does expected mean in this sense? | The answer written in pencil | A wrong answer on purpose | The last answer in the book | *The answer you predict before you work it out
test: «Sam was expecting a letter from his gran today.» What does expecting mean? | Running very fast | *Waiting for something to come | Sad and lonely | Asleep in bed
test: «Mum is expecting a new baby in the spring.» What does expecting mean here? | *Pregnant, going to have a baby | Playing a game | Moving house | Feeling cold
exam: «It was expected to rain all week.» What does expected mean? | Lost | Hidden | Forgotten | *Predicted, thought likely to happen
